e_formations_in_Zion_National_Park%2C_Utah.-_%28USA_2016%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Navajo_Sandstone_formations_in_Zion_National_Park,_Utah.-_(USA_2016).jpg","dist_m":285,"width":640,"height":490,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","artist":"Pierre André Leclercq"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Zyon_National_Parc_Crawford_place_%281%29.JPG/960px-Zyon_National_Parc_Crawford_place_%281%29.JPG","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zyon_National_Parc_Crawford_place_(1).JPG","dist_m":285,"width":640,"height":425,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","artist":"Pierre André Leclercq"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Zyon_National_Parc_Crowford_Arch_%281%29.jpg/960px-Zyon_National_Parc_Crowford_Arch_%281%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zyon_National_Parc_Crowford_Arch_(1).jpg","dist_m":285,"width":640,"height":360,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","artist":"© Pierre André"}],"street":null},{"id":"node/356672269","name":"Cable Mountain","kind":"peak","lon":-112.93355,"lat":37.26776,"ele_m":1969.0,"wikidata":"Q49017490","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_Mountain","tour":3,"summary":{"extract":"Cable Mountain is a 6,940-foot (2,120 m) elevation Navajo Sandstone summit located in Zion National Park, in Washington County of southwest Utah, United States. Towering 2,600 feet above the floor of Zion Canyon at the Big Bend area, Cable Mountain is situated immediately northeast of The Great White Throne, separated by the chasm of Hidden Canyon. It is set on the east side of the North Fork Virgin River which drains precipitation runoff from this mountain. Its neighbors include Angels Landing, Cathedral Mountain, The Organ, and Observation Point. This mountain's name was officially adopted in 1934 by the U.S. Board on Geographic Names. It is so named in association with the draw-works which used cables to lower timber from the top of the plateau down to the valley bottom from 1901 through 1927. Wood\nto construct the Zion Lodge came down the cable works. A 7.4-mile trail, much of it an old wagon road, leads to the views from the top.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cable_Mountain","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Washington_County%2C_UT%2C_USA_-_panoramio_%2844%29.jpg/960px-Washington_County%2C_UT%2C_USA_-_panoramio_%2844%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Washington_County,_UT,_USA_-_panoramio_(44).jpg","dist_m":92,"width":640,"height":480,"license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","artist":"halfuur"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/Zion_Misc%2C_Tree_With_View_5-1-14ha_%2814407824315%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zion_Misc,_Tree_With_View_5-1-14ha_(14407824315).jpg","dist_m":216,"width":640,"height":983,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"inkknife_2000 (7.5 million views +)"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Zion_Misc%2C_Evidence_of_Lava_5-1-14j_%2814221371687%29.jpg/960px-Zion_Misc%2C_Evidence_of_Lava_5-1-14j_%2814221371687%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zion_Misc,_Evidence_of_Lava_5-1-14j_(14221371687).jpg","dist_m":216,"width":640,"height":410,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"inkknife_2000 (7.5 million views +)"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Zion_Misc%2C_Trees_on_High_5-1-14i_%2814221214800%29.jpg/960px-Zion_Misc%2C_Trees_on_High_5-1-14i_%2814221214800%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zion_Misc,_Trees_on_High_5-1-14i_(14221214800).jpg","dist_m":216,"width":640,"height":481,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"inkknife_2000 (7.5 million views +)"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Zion_Misc%2C_Fly_Over_5-1-14_%2814406501462%29.jpg/960px-Zion_Misc%2C_Fly_Over_5-1-14_%2814406501462%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zion_Misc,_Fly_Over_5-1-14_(14406501462).jpg","dist_m":216,"width":640,"height":530,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"inkknife_2000 (7.5 million views +)"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Zion_Misc%2C_Hiking_5-1-14d_%2814221372077%29.jpg/960px-Zion_Misc%2C_Hiking_5-1-14d_%2814221372077%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zion_Misc,_Hiking_5-1-14d_(14221372077).jpg","dist_m":216,"width":640,"height":714,"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","artist":"inkknife_2000 (7.5 million views +)"}],"street":null},{"id":"node/356672290","name":"Castle Dome","kind":"peak","lon":-112.97077,"lat":37.26665,"ele_m":2141.0,"wikidata":"Q49018420","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castle_Dome_(Zion_National_Park)","tour":1,"summary":{"extract":"Castle Dome is a 7,054-foot (2,150 m) elevation Navajo Sandstone summit located in Zion National Park, in Washington County of southwest Utah, United States. Castle Dome is situated northwest of Zion Lodge, towering 2,800 feet (850 m) above the lodge and the floor of Zion Canyon. It is set on the west side of the North Fork Virgin River which drains precipitation runoff from this mountain. It is wedged between Behunin Canyon and Heaps Canyon, with the popular Emerald Pools set at the southeast foot of this mountain. Its neighbors include Mount Majestic, Cathedral Mountain, The Great White Throne, Red Arch Mountain, Mountain of the Sun, and Lady Mountain. This feature's name was officially adopted in 1934 by the U.S. Board on Geographic Names.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castle_Dome_(Zion_National_Park)","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[],"street":null},{"id":"node/356672303","name":"Cave Knoll","kind":"peak","lon":-113.10411,"lat":37.32081,"ele_m":1920.0,"wikidata":"Q49018786","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_Knoll","tour":0,"summary":{"extract":"Cave Knoll is a 6,486-foot (1,977 m) summit located in Zion National Park, in Washington County of southwest Utah, United States. Cave Knoll, a formation composed of Navajo Sandstone, is situated in Cave Valley, 11.5 mi (18.5 km) northwest of Springdale, Utah. Its neighbors include Pine Valley Peak, 1.7 mi (3 km) to the northeast, Tabernacle Dome, 1.6 mi (3 km) to the south-southeast, and North Guardian Angel, 2.5 mi (4 km) to the east. Precipitation runoff from this mountain drains into tributaries of the Virgin River. Access to this peak is via the Kolob Terrace Road. This peak's name was officially adopted in 1934 by the U.S. Board on Geographic Names.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cave_Knoll","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[],"street":null},{"id":"node/356672564","name":"Deertrap Mountain","kind":"peak","lon":-112.94383,"lat":37.23748,"ele_m":2054.0,"wikidata":"Q49024172","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deertrap_Mountain"},{"id":"node/356675877","name":"Isaac Peak","kind":"peak","lon":-112.97298,"lat":37.2448,"ele_m":2081.0,"wikidata":"Q49039194","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Peak"},{"id":"node/356673153","name":"Ivins Mountain","kind":"peak","lon":-113.00585,"lat":37.28719,"ele_m":2084.0,"wikidata":"Q49039282","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ivins_Mountain"},{"id":"node/356673284","name":"Johnson Mountain","kind":"peak","lon":-112.98633,"lat":37.17359,"ele_m":1859.0,"wikidata":"Q49040074","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnson_Mountain_(Utah)"},{"id"