e of the 229-square-mile (590 km2) park is Zion Canyon, which is 15 miles (24 km) long and up to 2,640 ft (800 m) deep. The canyon walls are reddish and tan-colored Navajo Sandstone eroded by the North Fork of the Virgin River. The park attracted 4,984,525 visitors in 2025.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zion_National_Park","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Wikipedia"},"photos":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Washington_County%2C_UT%2C_USA_-_panoramio_%2859%29.jpg/960px-Washington_County%2C_UT%2C_USA_-_panoramio_%2859%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Washington_County,_UT,_USA_-_panoramio_(59).jpg","dist_m":12,"width":640,"height":360,"license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","artist":"Mickey Løgitmark"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Washington_County%2C_UT%2C_USA_-_panoramio_%2862%29.jpg/960px-Washington_County%2C_UT%2C_USA_-_panoramio_%2862%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Washington_County,_UT,_USA_-_panoramio_(62).jpg","dist_m":15,"width":640,"height":360,"license":"CC BY 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","artist":"Mickey Løgitmark"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Utah_-_Zion_National_Park_-_Zion_Human_HIstory_Museum_-_Zion_Canyon_View_-_Fog_%2835868517875%29.jpg/960px-Utah_-_Zion_National_Park_-_Zion_Human_HIstory_Museum_-_Zion_Canyon_View_-_Fog_%2835868517875%29.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Utah_-_Zion_National_Park_-_Zion_Human_HIstory_Museum_-_Zion_Canyon_View_-_Fog_(35868517875).jpg","dist_m":19,"width":640,"height":431,"license":"CC BY 2.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","artist":"Jared"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/The_Witch_Head%2C_Alter_of_Sacrifice.jpg/960px-The_Witch_Head%2C_Alter_of_Sacrifice.jpg","page":"https://commons.wikimedi